<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n98203" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύλληψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύλλαψις</span></b> 
		v.l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			Heraclit.
			10
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>taking
				together, conjunction</i>, of sounds, <i><span class="en">
				Nicom.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; of two consonants, Sch.Heph.<i><span class="en">
				p.104
			</span></i> C., al.; <i>inclusion, comprehension</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				19.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Synt.</u>
				216.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				427
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συλλήψεως ἐπιρρήματα</span>
			(e.g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				642.14
			</span></i>; <i>summing up</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἀποδείξεων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					643.9
				</span></i>
			; <i>compendious statement</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. διὰ βραχέων τῆς ὅλης θεωρίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					18(2).848
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Rhet., <i>a
				figure by which a predicate belonging to one subject is
				attributed to several</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				p.100
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κατὰ-ψιν ὅρος</span>, i.e. embracing
			the adversary's counterplan as well as the original plan, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Stat.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, cf. Arg.<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>seizing, laying hold of, arresting, apprehending</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃστῶν ξ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.42.24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ξύλληψιν ποιεῖσθαι</span>
			<i>arrest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.134
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τήν τινος ς. κατασκευάσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.223
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				19.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. νεώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.46.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>conception, pregnancy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				582b11
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.23
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐν τῇ μῃτρὶ Ῥωμύλου
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόλαστοι ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				4.4.30
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>taking part with another, assistance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.808f
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
